Sat Nov 07 16:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Leave nouveau out of the initrd. It is blacklisted, and it pulled
  about 100 MB of nouveau GSP firmware into every initrd. With three
  kernels and two snapshots the 1 GB ESP filled up, sdbootutil gave
  the new snapshot only an entry for an old kernel, and that kernel
  has no NVIDIA module, so the desktop started without the driver.
- Release 7. The repository already has 0.1.0-6.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 07 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Set autoAgreeWithLicenses = yes in /etc/zypp/zypper.conf. Every
  package on download.nvidia.com carries a EULA, and transactional-update
  dup only passes --auto-agree-with-product-licenses. zypper answered
  "no" to the license and aborted with exit 4, so updates failed from
  Discover and from the command line.
- Release 6.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 23:01:47 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Ship the NVIDIA Tumbleweed repository at priority 200, and only with
  this package. Slowroll keeps libOpenCL1 and nvidia-libXNVCtrl.
  Agama installs the open G07 driver when the pattern is selected.
  First boot installs it only when those packages are missing.
- Do not require openSUSE-repos-Slowroll-NVIDIA. That service enables
  the same URL at the default priority.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 06:08:27 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Skip the first-boot install when the open G07 packages are already
  installed. Agama installs them when the NVIDIA pattern is selected.
- Release 4. The repository already has 0.1.0-2.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 05:15:42 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Mount the EFI partition from fstab before installing the driver.
  Inside the snapshot /boot is not that partition, so the kernel
  scriptlet fails, zypper exits 107, and transactional-update deletes
  the snapshot.
- Keep the snapshot when zypper exits 102 or 103. Those mean the
  packages were installed and a reboot is required.
- Write the install marker on the running system too. /var is a
  separate subvolume, so a marker written only in the snapshot stays
  hidden and the next boot installs the driver again.
- Release 4. The repository already has 0.1.0-2.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 04:48:53 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Pass --auto-agree-with-licenses after the zypper subcommand. zypper
  1.14 rejects it before the command, so the first-boot install exited
  2 and the driver was never installed.
- Reboot before the login screen once that snapshot is ready.
- Release 3. The repository already has 0.1.0-2.1.

